# HSM collector conformance v1 — Unix default-sensor catalog (#1414, part of epic #1413).
# No new verb: this fixture uses the existing `add_default_sensor|<id>` with two new stable ids,
#   unix_free_disk_space             -> managed UnixFreeSpaceOnDiskPrototype       / HSM_DEFAULT_UNIX_FREE_DISK_SPACE
#   unix_free_disk_space_prediction  -> managed UnixFreeSpaceOnDiskPredictionPrototype
#                                                                                  / HSM_DEFAULT_UNIX_FREE_DISK_SPACE_PREDICTION
# mapped in BOTH drivers (native DefaultSensorIdFromName, C# BuildDefaultSensorRequest).
#
# Why a separate fixture from default_sensors_contract: on a Unix host the disk sensor carries NO
# drive letter (one root mount), so it is a distinct catalog row whose NAME also changes the {name}
# the free-space alert template interpolates. That difference is exactly the thing a native Linux
# port could get wrong silently, so it is pinned here in both collectors.
#
# Registration is asserted by SUFFIX (see default_sensors_contract's header note): the native driver
# applies the collector's ComputerName/Module prefix while the C# driver records the prototype path.
# Description is NOT pinned; byte-exact parity for these two rows is additionally locked by the
# shared golden (tests/conformance/collector/golden/default_sensors_wire.golden), which the native
# native_default_sensors_wire_golden and the managed All_default_sensor_registrations_match_the_golden
# both reproduce.
#
# Both drivers run this on ANY OS: the registration payload is platform-agnostic text and the managed
# Unix prototypes construct without touching the filesystem. The LIVE READ side (which /proc file and
# which normalization each sensor uses) is not expressible in this protocol-level DSL; it is locked by
# the native algorithm-contract fixtures (proc_* in the native suite), whose sample inputs and expected
# numbers are copied verbatim from the managed ProcParsersTests — the same equivalence technique used
# for top-CPU (conformance_top_cpu_contract + cpu_select_top_n_*).

# Unix free space on disk — instant DoubleSensor, MB, EMA, IfEmaValue(<=,20480) + SensorError (Status 3).
# The name has NO drive letter, and the alert template interpolates that same letter-less name.
unix_free_disk_space_registers|create_collector
unix_free_disk_space_registers|add_default_sensor|unix_free_disk_space
unix_free_disk_space_registers|start
unix_free_disk_space_registers|stop
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_count|1
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|.computer/Disks monitoring/Free space on disk"
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"SensorType":2,
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"OriginalUnit":3,
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"DisplayUnit":0,
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"Statistics":1,
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"Property":210
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"Value":"20480"
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"Status":3,
unix_free_disk_space_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|Free space on disk is running out. Current free space is

# Unix free space prediction — TimeSpan, no data alert (Alerts:[] non-null empty list).
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|create_collector
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|add_default_sensor|unix_free_disk_space_prediction
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|start
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|stop
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|expect_registration_count|1
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|.computer/Disks monitoring/Free space on disk prediction"
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"SensorType":7,
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"Statistics":0,
unix_free_disk_space_prediction_registers|expect_registration_contains|0|"Alerts":[]

# The four sensors of the Unix computer set (UnixSensorsCollection.AddAllComputerSensors = system +
# disk) register side by side without colliding. This case registers them BY ID, so it pins the
# members and their coexistence, NOT the group helper's composition — that is guarded natively by
# native_default_sensor_group_composition (no group verb exists in the DSL today).
unix_computer_set_is_system_plus_disk|create_collector
unix_computer_set_is_system_plus_disk|add_default_sensor|total_cpu
unix_computer_set_is_system_plus_disk|add_default_sensor|free_ram
unix_computer_set_is_system_plus_disk|add_default_sensor|unix_free_disk_space
unix_computer_set_is_system_plus_disk|add_default_sensor|unix_free_disk_space_prediction
unix_computer_set_is_system_plus_disk|start
unix_computer_set_is_system_plus_disk|stop
unix_computer_set_is_system_plus_disk|expect_registration_count|4
